TCP vs UDP

This is very important.

TCP

TCP = Transmission Control Protocol

TCP is connection-oriented and provides reliable delivery.

Client ── SYN ──→ Server
Client ←─ SYN/ACK ─ Server
Client ── ACK ──→ Server
       Connection
       established

Examples:

SSH       → 22
HTTP      → 80
HTTPS     → 443
FTP       → 21
SMTP      → 25
MySQL     → 3306
PostgreSQL→ 5432
UDP

UDP = User Datagram Protocol

UDP is connectionless and generally faster, but it does not provide TCP-style delivery guarantees.

Examples:

DNS       → 53
DHCP      → 67/68
TFTP      → 69
NTP       → 123
SNMP      → 161
